  "level": 3,
  "question": {
    "text": "If $|w|=2$, then the set of points $z=w-\\frac{1}{w}$ is contained in or equal to the set of points $z$ satisfying",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "oNRNV",
      "text": "\r\n$\\operatorname{Im}(z)=0$\r\n",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "Y7keg",
      "text": "\r\n$|\\operatorname{Im}(z)| \\leq 1$\r\n",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "iaNZO",
      "text": "\r\n$|\\operatorname{Re}(z)| \\leq 2$\r\n",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "9j3ww",
      "text": "\r\n$|z| \\leq 3$",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "We have, $|w|=2 \\Rightarrow w=2(\\cos \\theta+i \\sin \\theta)$\r\n$\\therefore \\quad z=w-\\frac{1}{w}$\r\n$=2(\\cos \\theta+i \\sin \\theta)-\\frac{1}{2}(\\cos \\theta-i \\sin \\theta)$\r\n$\\Rightarrow \\quad z=\\frac{3}{2} \\cos \\theta+\\frac{5}{2} i \\sin \\theta$\r\n$\\Rightarrow \\quad|z|=\\sqrt{\\frac{9}{4}+\\frac{25}{4}}=\\frac{\\sqrt{17}}{2} < 3$\r\nHence, option (d) is correct.",
    "image": null
  },
